Subject: [Vita] io.c nogvl_wait_for must not reach select()

On an EAGAIN read or IO.copy_stream, io.c's select() build of
nogvl_wait_for calls rb_fd_select, which VitaSDK newlib implements with
sceNet epoll; the net library is never initialised, so it aborts at PC 0
(the same hazard the thread.c wait paths already close for
rb_thread_fd_select and rb_thread_wait_for_single_fd). This path runs
without the GVL and cannot raise, so it returns -1 with ENOSYS: IO#read then
falls back to the GVL-side wait, which raises NotImplementedError, and
IO.copy_stream raises Errno::ENOSYS.

--- a/io.c
+++ b/io.c
@@ -11429,6 +11429,16 @@
 
     int fd = fptr->fd;
     if (fd == -1) return 0;
+
+#if defined(__vita__)
+    /* rb_fd_select is select(), which this newlib implements via sceNet epoll
+     * (the net library is never initialised: prefetch abort at PC 0). This
+     * runs without the GVL, so fail with a plain errno; IO#read falls back to
+     * the GVL-side wait, which raises NotImplementedError, and IO.copy_stream
+     * raises Errno::ENOSYS. */
+    errno = ENOSYS;
+    return -1;
+#endif
 
     rb_fdset_t fds;
     int ret;
